ctive_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118400","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118400","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118400.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118400.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #118336\r\n\r\nWhen up_vector_sticky is true the up vector will try to align with the latest 'sticky' up vector. If the new frame's up vector difference is 90 degrees or more then it's up vector replaces the sticky up vector.\r\n\r\nThis eliminates roll in the curve even if it contains loops or other complex geometry.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118400/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118400/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}